  <!-- do_not_remove: published-with-gradle-metadata -->
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <groupId>de.scoopsoftware.cardlink</groupId>
  <artifactId>shared-android</artifactId>
  <version>2.2.0</version>
  <packaging>aar</packaging>
  <name>Cardlink SDK</name>
  <description>Cardlink SDK for Android — a Kotlin Multiplatform library enabling NFC-based German
health card (eGK) authentication and eHealth workflows.

The SDK provides a complete Cardlink flow implementation including:
• PACE protocol for NFC smart card authentication (eGK)
• Secure Messaging (SM) channel with automatic broken-channel detection and re-PACE
• Server-driven flow with REST session management and APDU relay
• PoPP (Proof of Patient Presence) mode for streamlined authentication
• WebSocket-based real-time card reading sessions
• OAuth 2.0 service with JWT decoding and credential storage
• APDU caching for improved performance in server-driven flows
• CAN persistence and known-cards management
• Session persistence across OAuth token expiry and app restarts
• Gzip decompression with performance metrics
• CameraX-based CAN scanner using ML Kit text recognition

Built with Kotlin Multiplatform (KMP), the SDK targets Android (this artifact)
and iOS (distributed as XCFramework via SPM). Platform bindings are available for
Flutter (scoop_cardlink) and React Native (@scoopsoftware/react-native-cardlink).

Version History:
• 1.2.49 — APDU caching in server-driven flow, PoPP mode, broken SM channel detection
• 1.2.46 — Swift Package Manager support, framework renamed to ScoopCardlink
• 1.2.43 — Basic Auth middleware with rate limiting
• 1.2.40 — Server-driven flow with REST session and APDU relay
• 1.2.35 — CardlinkFlow orchestration, NFC reader abstraction, session persistence
• 1.2.30 — SKIE integration for Swift async/await interoperability
• 1.2.25 — Cache providers for eGK card data
• 1.2.20 — WebSocket-based CardlinkSession for remote card reading
• 1.2.17 — OAuth service, JWT decoding, credential storage, device info</description>
